tƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarky"arXiv:2607.15314v1 Announce Type: new Abstract: Healthcare spans high-stakes communication, expert reasoning, and workflow execution, yet specialized LLMs that cover these use cases together remain limited. A healthcare model must handle patient consultation, clinical reasoning over text and images, interactive diagnosis, and electronic health record (EHR) tool use. These capabilities fail in different ways, and a narrow update for one task can degrade another. We present Cura 1T, a healthcare-specialized LLM trained through a human-gated self-evolution loop. In each evolution round, a training agent plans a target capability, trains the model, evaluates benchmark trajectories, and refines the data mixture from observed failures. This data-centered loop improves the model through targeted synthetic and curated examples rather than a single generic medical-data update. Across the healthcare evaluation suite, Cura 1T ranks at or near the top among frontier baselines, while remaining competitive on out-of-domain reasoning and agentic benchmarks.ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;9Qrt7vTbMtIxes-y6ONMTjau-OcUsYx3UZrhyWqvStoƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkx1Cura 1T: Specialized Model for Agentic Healthcareƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;Qbfp_9mXwvZhQya9XXZu1FDFfjRdNrEBV8ttcTajRMgƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkoSyndicationItemƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;DMPy79vjX51sdTRikvMYLEoThVtxQ_8SFuBmqML1KH4ƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkx https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.15314ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;WdTz0i1014Yg04wQIS8ZuaWdcrnVmYIyKtWQ_WEtPlAƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstard